//! Reference interpreter of RDNA 2 programs (wave32 and wave64): the Rust port of
//! `PrototypeScarlett/emu/rdna2_exec.py`. The Python stays the oracle: `tests/test_rdna2_ref_parity.py`
//! runs the same programs through both and compares the final state, instruction by instruction.
//!
//! Done: the decoder (`decode`, with the mnemonic table `mnemonics`, generated by
//! `tools/rdna2_ref_tables.py` from `emu/rdna2_ops.py`), the wave state (`wave`), the scalar
//! instructions, the branches and the program counter (`scalar`, `exec`, `pc`), the vector families
//! (`vector`, `compare`, `vop3`, `vop3p`, ...), the sparse global memory (`memory`), the scalar memory (`smem`), the integer
//! atomics (`atomic`), the LDS (`ds`, `ds_atomic`, `ds_half`, `ds_lanes`), FLAT, GLOBAL and SCRATCH
//! (`flat`, `vmem`), MUBUF (`mubuf`) and the typed buffer formats of MUBUF and MTBUF (`buffer_format`,
//! with the table `format_table` generated by the same tool, `format_convert`, `format_access`,
//! `format_exec`), and the 2D MIMG instructions (`image_desc`, `image_texel`, `image_sample`,
//! `image_exec`), and the graphics instructions: exports (`export`) and
//! interpolation (`interp`).

